From saphira@vm2.uk Thu Sep 17 00:00:00 2026
Subject: [PATCH] Saphira unmerged identity: bus default follows split-/run

Saphira is deliberately unmerged (real /bin, /sbin, /lib beside /usr/*)
with /var/run split from /run. Two gaps remain after the split-/run
patch, both stemming from upstream's merged-alias assumption:

- src/libsystemd/sd-bus/bus-internal.h: DEFAULT_SYSTEM_BUS_ADDRESS is
  hardcoded to /run/dbus/system_bus_socket with a comment stating the
  alias requirement outright. The daemon side already binds
  /var/run/dbus/system_bus_socket (derived from localstatedir), so
  every default client (logind, systemctl, busctl) looks in the wrong
  place and logind restart-loops at boot. Point the default at the
  daemon's address, derived the same way.
- src/core/taint.c: add an always-on "saphira-unmerged" taint entry so
  the status line names whose layout this is, instead of showing only
  upstream's merged-world diagnostics. The existing unmerged-usr and
  unmerged-bin checks are left intact (truthful signals); the stage
  array grows by one to hold the new entry.

Applies after saphira-split-run.patch (taint hunk contexts assume the
var-run removal); both orders were verified with --dry-run.

--- a/src/core/taint.c
+++ b/src/core/taint.c
@@ -33,7 +33,7 @@
 }
 
 char** taint_strv(void) {
-        const char *stage[11] = {};
+        const char *stage[12] = {};
         size_t n = 0;
 
         /* Returns a "taint string", e.g. "local-hwclock:var-run-bad". Only things that are detected at
@@ -41,6 +41,11 @@
          * configuration phase. */
 
         _cleanup_free_ char *bin = NULL, *usr_sbin = NULL;
+        /* Saphira identity: this build targets the deliberate unmerged
+         * layout (real /bin, /sbin, /lib beside /usr/*, split /var/run).
+         * This flag always fires: it declares build policy, not a runtime
+         * anomaly, so the status line names whose layout this is. */
+        stage[n++] = "saphira-unmerged";
 
         if (readlink_malloc("/bin", &bin) < 0 || !PATH_IN_SET(bin, "usr/bin", "/usr/bin"))
                 stage[n++] = "unmerged-usr";
--- a/src/libsystemd/sd-bus/bus-internal.h
+++ b/src/libsystemd/sd-bus/bus-internal.h
@@ -12,9 +12,12 @@
 #include "runtime-scope.h"
 #include "socket-util.h"
 
-/* Note that we use the new /run prefix here (instead of /var/run) since we require them to be aliases and
- * that way we become independent of /var being mounted */
-#define DEFAULT_SYSTEM_BUS_ADDRESS "unix:path=/run/dbus/system_bus_socket"
+/* Saphira split-layout: the system bus daemon binds
+ * /var/run/dbus/system_bus_socket (derived from localstatedir, the same
+ * way the daemon side derives it). The upstream /run default assumes a
+ * merged alias that does not exist here; default clients (logind,
+ * systemctl, busctl) would otherwise look in the wrong place. */
+#define DEFAULT_SYSTEM_BUS_ADDRESS "unix:path=/var/run/dbus/system_bus_socket"
 #define DEFAULT_USER_BUS_ADDRESS_FMT "unix:path=%s/bus"
 
 /* Private vtable flag: dispatch the method handler on its own fiber, so it can use suspending
